module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ConstantSheafQuotient
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ConstantSheafRingNaturality
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.KernelIdealSheaf

/-!
# The kernel ideal of a map of constant sheaves of rings

Let `(C, J)` be a site, let `π : Λ →+* Λ'` be a homomorphism of commutative rings and let
`α : Λ̲ ⟶ Λ'̲` be the induced morphism of constant sheaves of rings. This file computes the
sectionwise kernel of `α`: over every object `U` of the site,

`RingHom.ker α_U = (constantRingScalar J U '' ker π) · Γ(U, Λ̲)`,

the ideal of `Γ(U, Λ̲)` generated by the scalars of the elements of `ker π`. When `ker π` is
finitely generated as an ideal of `Λ` — and nothing more is assumed of `Λ` — that ideal is
finitely generated, which is the hypothesis `hI` of [Stacks, Tag 09BY] for the kernel ideal
sheaf `Stacks.SheafOfModules.kerIdeal α` of the reduction of a constant coefficient ring.

The inclusion `⊇` is formal: `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar_naturality` carries the
scalar of `a` to the scalar of `π a`, which vanishes when `a ∈ ker π`.

The inclusion `⊆` is the substantial one. It is the sectionwise half of [Stacks, Tag 093M] —
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSheaf_idealAction_sections_of_fg` — combined with the exactness of
`Γ(U, -)` on constant sheaves of modules, [Stacks, Tag 093J]. Both of those live in the category
of sheaves of `Λ`-modules, whereas `α` is a map of sheaves of *rings*; the comparison between the
two sides is `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv` below.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.ringHomToRestrictScalars`: a ring homomorphism `π : Λ →+* Λ'`, read as a
  `Λ`-linear map from `Λ` to `Λ'` with scalars restricted along `π`. This is the module-level
  analogue of `SheafOfModules.unitToRestrictScalarsObjUnit`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv`: **the base change comparison.** The sections
  over `U` of the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `Λ'` are the sections over `U` of the constant
  sheaf of rings `Λ'̲`, as abelian groups.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantValue`: the constant section of the constant
  sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `Λ` with value `a` is the scalar
  `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar J U a`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantModuleSheafMap`: the two sides of the base
  change square agree, as maps of abelian groups of sections.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv_map`: the comparison intertwines the map of
  module sections induced by `π` with `α` on sections.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.ker_constantSheaf_ringCatMap_app`: the sectionwise kernel of `α` is the
  ideal generated by the scalars of `ker π`, for a finitely generated `ker π`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.fg_ker_constantSheaf_ringCatMap_app` and
  `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.fg_kerIdeal_obj_constantSheaf_ringCatMap`: that ideal is finitely
  generated, the second statement in the form `[Stacks, Tag 09BY]` consumes — finite generation
  of the sections of `SheafOfModules.kerIdeal α` over every object.

## Implementation notes

**Why a comparison is needed at all.** `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingSectionsAddEquiv`
compares the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `Λ` with `Λ̲`, and so exists only at `M = Λ` over
`Λ`. The module side of the base change square lands in `Λ`-modules — the constant sheaf of
`Λ`-modules on `Λ'` — while the ring side lands in `Γ(U, Λ'̲)`. The missing edge is supplied here
by base change compatibility of `CategoryTheory.constantCommuteCompose` with
`forget₂ (ModuleCat Λ) AddCommGrpCat` against `forget₂ (ModuleCat Λ') AddCommGrpCat`: the
underlying abelian sheaf of the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on an `Λ`-module `M` is the constant
abelian sheaf on `M`, which is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.toSheafConstantIso`, and that
isomorphism is `Iso.refl`. So the two constant sheaves of modules — on `Λ'` over `Λ̲`, and on `Λ'`
over `Λ'̲` — have *the same* underlying abelian sheaf on the nose, and the comparison is
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSectionsAddEquiv` followed by
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.unitSectionsAddEquiv` over `Λ'`.

`Λ'` is taken as an abstract second ring with scalars restricted along `π`, rather than as a
quotient `Λ ⧸ I`, for two reasons: the `Λ`-module structure of
`(ModuleCat.restrictScalars π).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ' Λ')` has the same underlying abelian group as
the `Λ'`-module `Λ'` definitionally, which a quotient's own `AddCommGroup` instance need not; and
the consumer's reduction map is a composite of `Ideal.Quotient.mk` with universe-lifting ring
equivalences, so it is a general ring homomorphism whose kernel is the ideal in question.

**Where naturality is proved.** The compatibility
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantModuleSheafMap` cannot be checked section by
section: `Γ(U, Λ̲)` is not generated by the constant sections. It is instead an equality of two
morphisms of abelian *sheaves* out of a sheafification, hence determined by its composite with
`CategoryTheory.toSheafify` (`CategoryTheory.sheafify_hom_ext`), i.e. by its value on the constant
sections — and there
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantValue` and
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar_naturality` compute both sides as
`constantRingScalar J V (π a)`.

No route through `forget₂ RingCat AddCommGrpCat` preserving sheafification is used; the pinned
Mathlib does not provide it at an unrelated module universe, as recorded in the implementation
notes of `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ConstantSheafFiniteness`. The one place a
morphism of abelian sheaves underlying `α` is needed, it is written down by hand as the whiskering
of `α` with that forgetful functor, which asks nothing of sheafification.

**No Noetherian hypothesis.** Finite generation of `ker π` is all that is used, through
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSheaf_idealAction_sections_of_fg` and
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.fg_span_constantRingScalar_image`, matching [Stacks, Tag 09BY]. The adjacent
[Stacks, Tag 09BZ] does assume `Λ` Noetherian; that hypothesis is not imported here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09BY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09BY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 093J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 093M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093M)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.ConstantSheaf

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

section Scalar

variable {Λ : Type w} [CommRing Λ]
  [HasWeakSheafify J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  [J.PreservesSheafification (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J RingCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective RingCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- `constantRingSectionsAddEquiv` is `constantSectionsAddEquiv` followed by
`unitSectionsAddEquiv`. -/
private theorem constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_apply (U : C)
    (x : (constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)) :
    constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U x =
      unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U (constantSectionsAddEquiv J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) U x) :=
  rfl

/-- **The constant section with value `a` is the scalar of `a`.** The comparison
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.unitSectionsAddEquiv` carries the constant section of the constant sheaf of
`Λ`-modules on `Λ` with value `a` to `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar J U a`. -/
theorem unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantValue (U : C) (a : Λ) :
    unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U (constantValue J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) U a) =
      constantRingScalar J U a := by
  have hinv : ∀ t, (unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).symm t =
      ((unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ)).hom.val.app (op U)).hom t := fun _ => rfl
  have hval : constantValue J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) U 1 =
      (unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).symm 1 :=
    ((hinv 1).trans (unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf_hom_app_one J U)).symm
  have hone : constantSectionsAddEquiv J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) U
      ((constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).symm 1) =
      constantValue J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) U 1 := by
    rw [hval]
    refine (unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).injective ?_
    rw [AddEquiv.apply_symm_apply, ← constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_apply]
    exact (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).apply_symm_apply 1
  have hsm : ((a • 𝟙 (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)).hom : Λ →ₗ[Λ] Λ) 1 = a := by simp
  rw [constantRingScalar_eq, constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_apply, constantSectionsAddEquiv_smul,
    hone, constantValue_map_hom, hsm]

end Scalar

section BaseChange

variable {Λ : Type w} [CommRing Λ] {Λ' : Type w} [CommRing Λ'] (π : Λ →+* Λ')

/-- A ring homomorphism `π : Λ →+* Λ'`, read as a `Λ`-linear map from `Λ` to `Λ'` with scalars
restricted along `π`. The linearity is the computation `π (a * b) = π a * π b = a • π b`.

This is the module-level analogue of `SheafOfModules.unitToRestrictScalarsObjUnit`. -/
def ringHomToRestrictScalars :
    ModuleCat.of Λ Λ ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars π).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ' Λ') :=
  ModuleCat.homMk ((forget₂ RingCat.{w} AddCommGrpCat.{w}).map (RingCat.ofHom π))
    (fun r => by ext a; exact (π.map_mul r a).symm)

/-- The map `ringHomToRestrictScalars π` sends `a : Λ` to `π a`. -/
@[simp]
lemma ringHomToRestrictScalars_hom_apply (a : Λ) :
    (ringHomToRestrictScalars π).hom a = π a := rfl

/-- The kernel of `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.ringHomToRestrictScalars` is the kernel ideal of `π`,
read as a `Λ`-submodule of `Λ`. -/
lemma range_subtype_eq_ker_ringHomToRestrictScalars (I : Ideal Λ) (hker : RingHom.ker π = I) :
    LinearMap.range (ModuleCat.ofHom I.subtype).hom =
      LinearMap.ker (ringHomToRestrictScalars π).hom := by
  rw [ModuleCat.hom_ofHom, I.range_subtype]
  refine Submodule.ext fun a => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, ← hker, RingHom.mem_ker]
  exact Iff.rfl

variable [HasWeakSheafify J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  [J.PreservesSheafification (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ')]
  [J.PreservesSheafification (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ') AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ') AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J RingCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective RingCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **The base change square commutes on sections.** The map of sections of constant sheaves of
`Λ`-modules induced by `π`, followed by the comparison of the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on
`Λ'` with the constant sheaf of rings `Λ'̲`, is the map of sections of constant sheaves of rings
induced by `π`, preceded by the comparison over `Λ`.

The two sides are the components over `U` of two morphisms of abelian sheaves out of the constant
abelian sheaf on `Λ`, which is a sheafification; so it is enough to compare them on the constant
sections, where both are `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar J V (π a)`. -/
theorem unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantModuleSheafMap (U : C)
    (y : (constantModuleSheaf J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)).val.obj (op U)) :
    unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ') U
        ((constantModuleSheafMap J (ringHomToRestrictScalars π)).val.app (op U) y) =
      ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).map (RingCat.ofHom π)).hom.app (op U)
        (unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U y) := by
  let P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
    (Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj
      ((forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w}).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ))
  let T' := (SheafOfModules.toSheaf ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ'))).obj
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ')))
  let n₁ : sheafify J P ⟶ T'.val :=
    ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ))).map
        (unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ)).inv).hom ≫
      Functor.whiskerRight ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).map (RingCat.ofHom π)).hom
        (forget₂ RingCat.{w} AddCommGrpCat.{w})
  let n₂ : sheafify J P ⟶ T'.val :=
    ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ))).map
        (constantModuleSheafMap J (ringHomToRestrictScalars π))).hom ≫
      ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ'))).map
        (unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ')).inv).hom
  have hn : n₁ = n₂ := by
    refine sheafify_hom_ext J _ _ T'.property ?_
    ext V b
    show ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).map (RingCat.ofHom π)).hom.app (op V.unop)
          (unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) V.unop
            (constantValue J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) V.unop b)) =
        unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ') V.unop
          ((constantModuleSheafMap J (ringHomToRestrictScalars π)).val.app (op V.unop)
            (constantValue J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) V.unop b))
    rw [unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantValue, constantValue_map_hom]
    exact (constantRingScalar_naturality J π V.unop b).trans
      (unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantValue J (Λ := Λ') V.unop (π b)).symm
  exact (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (NatTrans.congr_app hn (op U)) y).symm

/-- **The base change comparison.** The sections over `U` of the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on
`Λ'`, scalars restricted along `π`, are the sections over `U` of the constant sheaf of rings
`Λ'̲`, as abelian groups.

Both are the sections of the constant abelian sheaf on the additive group of `Λ'`: the first by
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSectionsAddEquiv` over `Λ`, the second by
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.unitSectionsAddEquiv` over `Λ'`, and the two constant sheaves of modules
have the same underlying abelian sheaf on the nose. -/
def baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv (U : C) :
    ((constantSections J U).obj
        ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars π).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ' Λ'))) ≃+
      (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ')).obj.obj (op U)) :=
  (constantSectionsAddEquiv J ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars π).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ' Λ')) U).trans
    (unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ') U)

/-- The base change comparison intertwines the map of module sections induced by `π` with the map
of ring sections induced by `π`. -/
theorem baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv_map (U : C)
    (t : (constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)) :
    baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv J π U
        (((constantSections J U).map (ringHomToRestrictScalars π)).hom t) =
      ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).map (RingCat.ofHom π)).hom.app (op U)
        (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U t) := by
  show unitSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ') U
      (constantSectionsAddEquiv J ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars π).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ' Λ')) U
        (((constantSections J U).map (ringHomToRestrictScalars π)).hom t)) = _
  rw [constantSectionsAddEquiv_map, constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_apply,
    unitSectionsAddEquiv_constantModuleSheafMap J π U]

end BaseChange

section Kernel

variable {Λ : Type w} [CommRing Λ] {Λ' : Type w} [CommRing Λ'] (π : Λ →+* Λ')

variable [HasSheafify J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)] [HasWeakSheafify J (Type w)]
  [J.PreservesSheafification (forget (ModuleCat.{w} Λ))]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget (ModuleCat.{w} Λ))]
  [J.PreservesSheafification (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ')]
  [J.PreservesSheafification (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ') AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ') AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J RingCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective RingCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **The sectionwise kernel of a map of constant sheaves of rings.** Over every object `U` of
the site, the kernel of the ring homomorphism `α_U : Γ(U, Λ̲) → Γ(U, Λ'̲)` induced by
`π : Λ →+* Λ'` is the ideal of `Γ(U, Λ̲)` generated by the scalars of the elements of the kernel
ideal `I` of `π`.

The inclusion `⊇` is `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar_naturality`. The inclusion `⊆` is
the sectionwise half of [Stacks, Tag 093M] for a finitely generated ideal,
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSheaf_idealAction_sections_of_fg`, together with the exactness of
`Γ(U, -)` on constant sheaves of modules, [Stacks, Tag 093J], transported along
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv`. Only finite generation of `I` is used; `Λ` is
an arbitrary commutative ring. -/
theorem ker_constantSheaf_ringCatMap_app (I : Ideal Λ) (hker : RingHom.ker π = I) (hI : I.FG)
    (U : C) :
    RingHom.ker (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).map (RingCat.ofHom π)).hom.app (op U)).hom =
      Submodule.span (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U))
        (constantRingScalar J U '' (I : Set Λ)) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · intro x hx
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker] at hx
    set t := (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).symm x with ht
    have hxt : constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U t = x :=
      (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).apply_symm_apply x
    have hzero : baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv J π U
        (((constantSections J U).map (ringHomToRestrictScalars π)).hom t) = 0 := by
      rw [baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv_map, hxt, hx]
    have hker' : ((constantSections J U).map (ringHomToRestrictScalars π)).hom t = 0 := by
      refine (baseChangeSectionsAddEquiv J π U).injective ?_
      rw [hzero, map_zero]
    have hexact := range_constantSections_map_eq_ker J U (ModuleCat.ofHom I.subtype)
      (ringHomToRestrictScalars π)
      (range_subtype_eq_ker_ringHomToRestrictScalars π I hker)
    have hmem : t ∈ LinearMap.range
        ((constantSections J U).map (ModuleCat.ofHom I.subtype)).hom := by
      rw [hexact, LinearMap.mem_ker]
      exact hker'
    rw [constantSheaf_idealAction_sections_of_fg J I hI U] at hmem
    have := mem_span_constantRingScalar_of_mem_smul_top J I U hmem
    rwa [hxt] at this
  · rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro z ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
    have hπa : π a = 0 := by
      rw [← RingHom.mem_ker, hker]
      exact ha
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, constantRingScalar_naturality, hπa,
      constantRingScalar_zero]

/-- **Finite generation of the sectionwise kernel.** If the kernel ideal of `π : Λ →+* Λ'` is
finitely generated, then the kernel of `α_U : Γ(U, Λ̲) → Γ(U, Λ'̲)` is a finitely generated ideal
of `Γ(U, Λ̲)`, over every object `U` of the site. No condition on `Λ` beyond that finite
generation is used. -/
theorem fg_ker_constantSheaf_ringCatMap_app (I : Ideal Λ) (hker : RingHom.ker π = I) (hI : I.FG)
    (U : C) :
    (RingHom.ker
      (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).map (RingCat.ofHom π)).hom.app (op U)).hom).FG := by
  rw [ker_constantSheaf_ringCatMap_app J π I hker hI U]
  exact fg_span_constantRingScalar_image J I hI U

/-- **The hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 09BY] for a constant coefficient ring.** The sections over
every object of the kernel ideal sheaf of a map of constant sheaves of rings are finitely
generated, as soon as the kernel ideal of the ring homomorphism is.

This is the form the consumer wants: the hypothesis `hI` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.isZero_of_isDerivedComplete_of_idealProduct_eq_top` asks for
`(I.toSubmodule.obj (op U)).FG`, and for `I = SheafOfModules.kerIdeal α` that submodule is
`RingHom.ker α_U` by `SheafOfModules.kerIdeal_obj`. -/
theorem fg_kerIdeal_obj_constantSheaf_ringCatMap (I : Ideal Λ) (hker : RingHom.ker π = I)
    (hI : I.FG) (U : C) :
    ((SheafOfModules.kerIdeal
      ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).map (RingCat.ofHom π))).obj (op U)).FG := by
  rw [SheafOfModules.kerIdeal_obj]
  exact fg_ker_constantSheaf_ringCatMap_app J π I hker hI U

end Kernel

end Stacks.ConstantSheaf

end
